 SSH Troubleshooting Scenarios (Real Production Cases)

1. SSH Connection Refused
Error:
ssh: connect to host <ip> port 22: Connection refused
Root Cause:
-- SSH service not running
-- Port blocked

Fix:
-- systemctl status sshd
-- systemctl start sshd

ss -tulnp | grep ssh
firewall-cmd --list-all


2. Permission Denied (Publickey)
Error:
Permission denied (publickey).

Root Cause:
-- Wrong key / key not copied
-- Permission issue

Fix:
chmod 700 ~/.ssh
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys

ssh-copy-id user@server


3. Too Many Authentication Failures
Error:
Received disconnect: Too many authentication failures

Root Cause:
SSH trying multiple keys

Fix:
ssh -i id_rsa user@server

OR edit:
~/.ssh/config
IdentitiesOnly yes


4. Host Key Verification Failed
Error:
WARNING: REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION HAS CHANGED!

Root Cause:
Server reinstalled / key changed

Fix:
ssh-keygen -R <server_ip>

5. Connection Timeout
Error:
ssh: connect to host <ip> port 22: Connection timed out

Root Cause:
Network issue / firewall

Fix:
ping <ip>
telnet <ip> 22
firewall-cmd --list-ports


6. Slow SSH Login
Root Cause:

DNS lookup delay

Fix:
Edit config:
UseDNS no

Restart:
systemctl restart sshd


7. Key-based login not working but password works
Root Cause:
-- Pubkey disabled

Fix:
PubkeyAuthentication yes
AuthorizedKeysFile .ssh/authorized_keys


8. SSH hangs after login
Root Cause:
-- .bashrc / profile issue

Fix:
ssh -t user@server bash --noprofile --norc

Check:
~/.bashrc
~/.bash_profile


9. SELinux blocking SSH key access (RHEL)
Root Cause:
-- wrong context

Fix:
restorecon -Rv ~/.ssh

OR:
ls -Z ~/.ssh


10. User unable to SSH but exists
Root Cause:
-- shell disabled

Check:
cat /etc/passwd | grep user

Fix:
usermod -s /bin/bash user


