5. What is difference between system cron and user cron ?

✅ User Cron (crontab -e)

Created using crontab -e command
Stored per user (each user has separate cron)
No need to mention user in job
Runs with permissions of that user
Location: /var/spool/cron/<username>

👉 Example:
* * * * * /home/user/script.sh


✅ System Cron (/etc/crontab)
Defined in system-wide cron file
Managed by admin/root
Must specify user in job
Used for system-level tasks

Location:
/etc/crontab
/etc/cron.d/

👉 Example:
* * * * * root /root/script.sh


6. How to schedule job every specific interval ?
Examples:
*/5 * * * * script.sh     # every 5 minutes
0 */2 * * * script.sh     # every 2 hours
0 0 */3 * * script.sh     # every 3 days


7. How to redirect cron output to file (VERY IMPORTANT)?
* * * * * script.sh >> /var/log/script.log 2>&1

👉 Explanation:

>> → append output
2>&1 → include errors


8. How to troubleshoot cron jobs not running ?
Check service:
systemctl status crond

Check logs:
tail -f /var/log/cron        # RHEL
tail -f /var/log/syslog      # Ubuntu

Check:
correct path
permissions
script executable


9. Why cron jobs fail sometimes ?
Common reasons:
PATH not defined
permission issue
wrong syntax
service not running

Fix (set PATH):
PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin


10. What is difference between cron and anacron ?

✅ Cron

Used for scheduled recurring jobs (exact time execution)
Runs only if system is ON at scheduled time
If system is OFF → job is missed/skipped
Suitable for servers (always running systems)
Supports minute-level precision

👉 Example:
0 2 * * * backup.sh    # runs at 2 AM (only if system is ON)


✅ Anacron

Used for delayed job execution
Runs jobs even if system was OFF earlier
Executes missed jobs when system comes back online
Suitable for laptops / desktops
Works with day-level scheduling (not minute level)

👉 Config file:
/etc/anacrontab


✅ Quick Difference (One-Line Memory)

Cron → runs on exact time, skips if missed
Anacron → runs later if missed due to system downtime

11. What is @daily, @hourly in cron ?
Shortcuts:
@reboot script.sh      # runs at system startup
@daily script.sh       # once per day
@hourly script.sh      # every hour
@weekly script.sh      # once per week
@monthly script.sh     # once per month


12. How to restrict users from using cron ?
Files:
/etc/cron.allow
/etc/cron.deny

Rules:
If cron.allow exists → only listed users allowed
Else → cron.deny users blocked


13. How to run cron job as another user ?
System cron:
* * * * * user script.sh


14. How to schedule job at reboot ?
@reboot /path/script.sh

